                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "D'LIRIUM is probably one of the best games ever. i love the horror-pony theme and the combat system and story is amazing.\r\nThe atmosphere is really good as well. it really was memorable to me and so much fun finding all the secrets. the devs really did a good job with making it real creepy and eerie. everything has so much detail that i couldnt believe this was 5 euros.\r\nExploring the levels and clearing all the monsters with various types of weapons and magic is quite fun and doesnt bore you quickly. The variety of melee weapons and magic spells you could use to fight monsters are very refreshing so its not some lame 1 attack for the whole game type of deal. \r\nThe game itself has various difficulties if you ever want to challenge yourself. they also have easier difficulties if youre not the best at games.\r\nachievement hunting was EXTREMELY fun in this game. (i need one more achievement that is seasonal to complete the game fully)\r\nit never felt like a chore to me because the game is filled with so much stuff and although some of the achievements are a bit challenging it never stopped me from playing-it only encouraged me to continue. I really like how the devs made it so that you could enter a command in the console (map gestas) and visit a different map to explore.\r\nI could replay this game quite a bit, and i have for the achievements and solely for fun. i think its definitely something you could come back to and have a blast playing again.\r\nIn the end, i would 100% reccomend this game to anyone who loves ponies, and id even reccomend it to those who dont because the game itself is really well made. if you are considering this game even in the slightest, then you should go buy it.\r\n",
